+#### Learner state: ephemeral vs durable
+
+The `/learn/*` surface is identical in both modes; only survival differs.
+
+| | `ZSM_MASTER_KEK` unset (default) | `ZSM_MASTER_KEK` set |
+|---|---|---|
+| store | in-memory `Map` (`src/learn-store.ts`) | `@zsm/store` — PGlite Postgres, append-only `learner_event`, per-learner DEK, FORCE-RLS (`src/durable-learn-store.ts`) |
+| survives a restart | **no** | **yes**, from `ZSM_DATA_DIR` |
+| boot line | `[@zsm/api] learner state EPHEMERAL — set ZSM_MASTER_KEK for durability` | `[@zsm/api] learner state DURABLE — PGlite dataDir=…` |
+| crypto-shred | n/a | admin-only (`AppInstance.durable.erase`, no HTTP surface); a shredded learner answers **`410`** on every `/learn` route, and the anonymous population statistics are untouched |
+
+```bash
+# generate a key (keep it out of the repo — losing it means losing every learner's state, by design)
+export ZSM_MASTER_KEK=$(node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))")
+export ZSM_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/zsm/data
+pnpm --filter @zsm/api start
+```
+
+Mastery is reproduced EXACTLY across a restart, and durable mode folds with the same options as ephemeral
+mode, so switching the env never changes a learner's numbers (`test/durable-learn.test.ts`).
+
